When `num_tokens` is 0, calling `torch_npu.npu_transpose_batchmatmul` with an empty tensor can lead to undefined behavior or runtime errors on Ascend NPUs. We should add a guard to return an empty tensor directly when `num_tokens == 0`.

```python
    num_tokens = x.shape[0]
    if num_tokens == 0:
        return x.new_empty(0, x.shape[1], w.shape[-1])
    if num_tokens <= chunk:
        return torch_npu.npu_transpose_batchmatmul(x, w, **perm)
```

